Participative internship at ING Corporate Finance Mid-Market 
 ING is looking for an intern for the Corporate Finance Mid-Market department in Amsterdam. Corporate Finance Mid-Market is the team that provides specialist corporate finance (M&A) advice to ING’s Business Banking customers on acquisitions and business transfers worth €15-200 million. The CFMM team currently consists of 15 people.
 Roles and responsibilities 
 The intern will be a full member of the Corporate Finance Mid-Market team during the internship period. The internship’s objective is therefore to introduce the intern to ING’s advisory practice in the full breadth of its services. The intern has the opportunity of participating as a full team member in strategically advising customers on business transfers.
 During the internship period, the intern will perform the following tasks:
• participating in the compilation of strategic pitches for customers and prospects;
• participating in writing information memoranda for sales transactions;
• participating in the preparation of longlists of potential buyers;
• participating in company valuations (Excel model and reporting);
• supporting the team in the entire transaction process;
• preparing negotiations with potential buyers.
 How to succeed 
 We hire smart people like you for your potential. Our biggest expectation is that you’ll stay curious. Keep learning. Take on responsibility. In return, we’ll back you to develop into an even more awesome version of yourself.
• an enterprising, energetic, ambitious student with above average grades;
• university master’s student in business economics, business administration, economics or finance;
• extensive knowledge of various valuation methods, Excel and PowerPoint;
• strong analytical and numerical skills, result-oriented;
• motivated team player, eager to learn and hands-on;
• stress-resistant, strong drive and ambition;
• ability to perform excellently under time pressure;
• affinity with mergers and acquisitions;
• interested in Mid-Market companies, director/majority shareholders and family businesses;
• excellent command of written and spoken Dutch and English;
• advantage: commercial affinity, entrepreneurial and self-motivating.
 Rewards and benefits 
 This is a great opportunity to train with highly skilled people who are experts in their field. You’ll do a lot and learn a lot – not only about your specialist area and the bank, but also about yourself and whether this type of environment is right for you.
 You’ll also benefit from:
• Internship allowance of 700 EUR based on 36 hours work week
• Your own work laptop
• Hybrid working to blend home working for focus and office working for collaboration and co-creation
• Personal growth and challenging work with endless possibilities
• An informal working environment with innovative colleagues
 During the duration of your internship at ING, it is mandatory to be enrolled at a Dutch university (or EU-university for EU passport holders).
 Applications 
 Click the application button and upload your CV, letter of application and grade sheets from secondary school and university to apply immediately. For more information about ING, please visit: www.ing.nl/werken .
 About our internships 
 Every year, more than 350 students join our internship program. While there are no guarantees about your future, many of our former interns move into a permanent role or onto our International Talent Programme (traineeship).
 Whatever happens

PJT Partners is a global advisory-focused investment bank. Our team of senior professionals delivers a wide array of strategic advisory, shareholder advisory, restructuring and special situations and private fund advisory and placement services to corporations, financial sponsors, institutional investors and governments around the world. We offer a unique portfolio of advisory services designed to help our clients achieve their strategic objectives. We also provide, through PJT Park Hill, private fund advisory and fundraising services for alternative investment managers, including private equity funds, real estate funds and hedge funds.
 From the beginning, PJT Partners has firmly believed that having the best people is key to building an enduring franchise. Our perspective was, and remains, that a great team brings in both top tier clients and appeals to a wide-range of diverse, talented colleagues. Fostering an inclusive culture, which welcomes differing perspectives and beliefs, enables us to provide the best advice and insights to our clients.
 To learn more about PJT Partners, please visit our website at www.pjtpartners.com . 
 Responsibilities 
 PJT Park Hill is seeking an experienced industry professional for its Infrastructure Distribution Team. The ideal candidate will possess strong leadership, interpersonal, client management, and analytical and writing skills, as well as demonstrate exemplary work ethic, attention to detail, mentorship, and the ability to work well both independently and within teams.
 Responsibilities include:
• Provide expert product and market content as a trusted advisor to PJT Park Hill clients;
• Embrace a culture of collaboration and teamwork;
• Have a willingness to travel extensively, keep meticulous records and work closely with the US based distribution and project management teams as well as senior partners;
• Understand the differentiated investment processes across our client base, following up and closing on commitments.
 Qualifications 
 PJT Partners seeks to hire individuals who are highly motivated, intelligent and have demonstrated excellence in prior endeavors. In addition, qualified candidates will possess the following:
• Experience selling various private markets strategies and the ability to articulate the risk/reward spectrum across these strategies;
• Passion for private markets and a strong understanding of the private markets investment and LP buyer landscape;
• Strategic thinker, with appreciation and understanding for where the private markets funds are and where they are headed in the US and globally;
• Natural relationship builder and ability to “read the room” and adapt one’s messaging and conversation based on the audience and investor appetite;
• Technical product knowledge; ability to quickly understand and articulate a GP’s investment strategy / strategies in technical depth;
• Strong, established relationships with North American and global infrastructure companies and key decision-makers within the firms;
• Demonstrable track record of building client relationships;
• Ability to work in a fast paced, dynamic environment and to handle multiple projects at a time;
• Confident and self-aware with excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal;
• Strong work ethic, passion for excellence, results-oriented;
• Personal and professional integrity of the highest order;
• Self starter who takes initiative and is collaborative both internally and extern

